00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.520
Greetings fellow earthlings today we're going to talk about the technology

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.180
within Star Trek that has become true today.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.230
Star Trek is known for predicting tons of technological achievements, such as:

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.820
cell phones, bluetooth, flat screen tvs, 

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.380
Skype, iPads, and talking computers.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.150
"Hello computer."  All of these gadgets exist in the Star Trek universe

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.490
far before they became a reality and now we're gonna update you on the new 

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:25.700
developments in technology.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.120
The first item on our list is something you probably already heard of

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.100
"Virtual Display" AKA Google Glass. In Star Trek members the super evil group

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.420
"the Dominion" didn't bother using flat screen monitors to surf the web but 

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.310
trippy looking headsets with one eye piece

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:43.120
that projected computer imagery through their optic nerve and into their brain.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.310
They could watch streaming video of the outside of the ship, receive messages.,

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:50.250
and video chat with other evil Dominion leaders just like Google Glass.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.390
Next, let's revisit a classic that finally being made today.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:58.370
"The Medical Tricorder." That would prove to have virtually no limitations in terms of scanning

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.310
It is most famous for its ability to diagnose pretty much anything.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:03.070
"Sever theta radiation poisoning."

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:06.880
Today's equivalent of tricorders are capable of diagnosing most ailments.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.230
in the human body without needing to see a doctor. 

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:12.160
Just by placing on your left temple, the Scanadu Scout

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.510
can provide results for pulse transit time, heart rate

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:16.270
temperature, blood oxygenation and more.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:19.200
Diagnosing anything from abdominal cramps to shingles,

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.840
it's quite an upgrade from your thermometer.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.360
Next up on our list, an overlooked essential for all interstellar space travel.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.410
 "transparent aluminum?"

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.760
what do you think space windows were made of? 

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.810
When the Enterprise crew traveled back to 1986

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.210
Scotty handed over the formula for creating the super-strong, yet incredibly thin glass

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.030
that proved to hold up against nearly everything the universe threw at it.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.200
"That's the ticket laddie." 

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.550
Due to Scotty's interference with the timeline,

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:46.480
 the transparent aluminum armor is now marketed as "Alon" 

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:47.950
by the Surmet corporation. 

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:52.640
The armor can resist a fifty-caliber armor-piercing bullet and anti-aircraft weapons

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.980
all while being half the weight and thickness of typical bullet-proof glass.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.390
Okay, let's move on to something that will truly change your life.

